  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 1032822,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 12th Sector Music: A Commodore 64 Symphony of Survival\n\nIn *12th Sector Music*, you're not just playing a game – you're composing the soundtrack to a desperate struggle. Set in a ravaged future, humanity clings to existence within a series of orbital habitats, the 12th Sector. A catastrophic solar flare has crippled the sector's defenses, leaving it vulnerable to relentless robotic scavengers known as the \"Harmonics.\"\n\nGameplay revolves around a unique blend of music creation and strategic defense. Using a simplified, intuitive interface reminiscent of early music composition software (like IGDB), you craft musical sequences that directly power your habitat's shields and weaponry.  Each note, chord, and rhythm corresponds to a defensive action – a burst of energy, a targeting lock, or a repair sequence. \n\nBut beware! The Harmonics adapt to your musical patterns.  Experimentation and creativity are key to outsmarting them.  Successfully defend your habitat, unlock new musical elements, and uncover the secrets behind the solar flare in this challenging and innovative Commodore 64 experience. Can you compose your way to survival?"
    },
